# ─── Go ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.prof
coverage.out
coverage.html
/pgsheet
/pgsheet.exe
/pgsheet-cli
/pgsheet-cli.exe
vendor/
go.work
go.work.sum

# ─── Wails / build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The whole build directory is ignored. Everything in it is either output
# (build/bin), vendored (the ~130MB WebView2 payload) or regenerated by wails
# on each build, and wails has already deleted a hand-written file placed there
# once. Anything that must survive a clone lives in scripts/ instead:
#   the icon      -> build/appicon.png, regenerate with `go run ./scripts/genicon`
#   the NSIS include -> scripts/installer/webview2-offline.nsh
/build/
frontend/dist/*
!frontend/dist/.gitkeep
# Generated by wails on every build. Never edited, so never committed.
frontend/wailsjs/

# ─── Frontend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.npm/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ─── IDE / editor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp

# ─── OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ─── Operator data — must never reach the repository ──────────────────
# Real client spreadsheets, generated import scripts, logs and credentials.
# Test fixtures under testdata/ are the deliberate exception.
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv
!testdata/**
*.generated.sql
/out/
/local/
logs/
.env
.env.*
*.pgpass
pgsheet.log*
# Half-written configurations from an interrupted save.
.pgsheet-*.tmp

# ─── Signing / notarization secrets ───────────────────────────────────
*.p12
*.pfx
*.cer
*.provisionprofile
notarytool-*.json

# ─── Local working files, not part of the repository ──────────────────
# Kept on the working machine by choice.
/docs/

# Working instructions for Claude Code.
/CLAUDE.md

# Fixture workbooks and schemas for manual testing. Note this is anchored to
# the repository root: internal/sqlgen/testdata holds the golden files that
# `go test ./...` compares against, and those stay tracked.
/testdata/

# ─── Claude Code local overrides ──────────────────────────────────────
.claude/settings.local.json

# ─── Specification working documents (kept local, not tracked) ─────────
/plan/
